  id: Cleidocephalic_muscle_Brachiocephalic_muscle.R
  partName: Cleidocephalic muscle Brachiocephalic muscle R
  descriptionChunks:
  - 'This muscle is part of the brachiocephalic group and is responsible for extending
    the head and neck forward. It plays an important role in locomotion by assisting
    in forward movement of the body. '
  - It also helps maintain posture by stabilizing the head during motion. The muscle
    works in coordination with limb muscles to ensure efficient and balanced movement,
    particularly during walking, running, or other dynamic activities.
